    "result_text": "The build is green. All tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the read-only `timezone` field on the Owner API, derived from the owner's locality/region via a fixed region-to-timezone table, following the existing `locality` pattern in this Spring Boot app.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` property (read-only string, IANA name) to the `Owner` schema, right after `locality`. The OpenAPI generator picks this up to produce `getTimezone`/`setTimezone` on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/RegionTimezones.java`** (new) \u2014 A single source of truth for the fixed region-to-timezone table (`NSW->Australia/Sydney, VIC->Australia/Melbourne, QLD->Australia/Brisbane`), mirroring the existing `CityRegions` util. `timezoneOf(region)` returns `null` for unmapped regions.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `timezone` plus a `toTimezone(owner)` default method that reuses `toLocality(owner)` and looks the region up in `RegionTimezones`, keeping `timezone` and `locality` in lock-step. Returns `null` (field omitted) when the region has no mapped timezone.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
