    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established idioms cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The region\u2192timezone table lands in its own `RegionTimezones` util class, directly parallel to the existing `CityRegions` and `PostcodeRules` \"single source of truth\" table classes (same `final` class + private constructor + `Map.of` + static lookup returning `null` on miss + matching Javadoc shape). It is correctly *not* bolted onto `PostcodeRules`, whose concern is postcode ranges/region resolution \u2014 a distinct responsibility.\n\n- **No duplication.** `toTimezone` derives the region by calling the existing `toLocality(owner)` rather than re-resolving it, so timezone stays in lock-step with locality exactly as the Javadoc promises. No region-derivation logic is copied.\n\n- **Consistent mapper structure.** `toTimezone` mirrors the sibling `default` derivation methods (`toLocality`, `toContactPreference`, `toTelephoneDisplay`), each a thin delegation to a util with a null-means-omit contract, and the `@Mapping` entry is placed logically right after `locality`. The OwnerMapper interface is not becoming a catch-all \u2014 the real logic stays in the util class.\n\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` schema addition matches the neighboring read-only derived fields in style and placement.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this a natural extension of the existing pattern.",
